    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0683" n="583" xml:id="pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/537: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-12T19:00:00+02:00">April 12, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 12—5:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Insull, accompanied by Colonel Crane and Berry, in custody Turkish officials
                    departed 7 p.m. by steamer for Izmir, expecting to transfer to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Exilona</hi> Friday evening.<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d500-f1"/> Please have Berry relieved of responsibility at
                    quarantine New York informing him regarding identifying documents of relieving
                    officer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
